gm-method (a panel whose imperative host elements are wiped-and-recreated by an "ensure hosts" guard keyed on isConnected silently loses any one-time paint done into a host that gets recreated, whenever the container starts DETACHED and mounts later): a tab-body container built before its tab mounts has isConnected=false, so every data-driven refresh (setX -> renderList -> ensureHosts) tears down and recreates the host pair, discarding whatever a construction-time render painted into the sibling host (a toolbar) while only repainting the list -- the toolbar then stays empty forever because nothing ever repaints it after mount. The witness signature: an empty <div></div> where a toolbar should be, beside a fully-populated sibling list. Fix pattern: any ensure-hosts guard that can RECREATE hosts must also re-run every one-time paint that targets those hosts (call renderToolbar inside ensureHosts after recreation), never rely on a single construction-time paint surviving. Diagnosis path that found it: dump each candidate panel's firstElementChild.outerHTML live (empty-div tell), after first eliminating stale-module-cache via CDP Network.clearBrowserCache + setCacheDisabled and a served-source fetch(cache:no-store) content check -- the cache-elimination step matters because a stale ES-module map produces the identical symptom.